**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests`

**How to implement.** A zip or an unzip runs off the UI thread with per-file progress and Cancel, through `JobRunner`, and the two dialogs open (.spec-md §10.2: 'Per item: … one zipped file. Each shows a progress bar with Cancel, through JobRunner'; §10.3: one click with Cancel; §6 'Long work: OpticalConstructor.Ui/JobRunner.fs'; the S6 brief: Send kit… through a save dialog defaulting to the exports folder). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob`, compiled directly after `KitOpening.fs` (step 150), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6. (1) `type KitArchiveFileCount with member this.jobStepCount : JobStepCount` (`JobRunner.fs:JobStepCount`), a file count as the runner's step count; `type KitArchiveProgress with member this.jobProgress (elapsed : JobElapsed) : JobProgress` is `{ completed = this.filesDone.jobStepCount; total = Some this.filesTotal.jobStepCount; elapsed = elapsed }` (`JobRunner.fs:JobProgress`). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveJobHandle = { cancelArchiveJob : unit -> unit }`, how a started job is cancelled. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveJobHost = { startArchiveJob : (KitArchiveObserver -> Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>) -> KitArchiveJobHandle }`: starts one archive job (step 197) and answers its handle; the job's progress and its end reach the two callbacks the host was built with. (a) `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError> -> unit) : KitArchiveJobHost` makes a `CancellationTokenSource` per job and runs the job through `JobRunner.startBackground` (`JobRunner.fs:154`) on a thread-pool worker, as `RanToCompletion [ <the job's result> ]`. Its observer's `reportArchiveProgress p` calls `post (fun () -> progressed (p.jobProgress <the elapsed time of a Stopwatch started with the job>))`, and `onDone` calls `post (fun () -> ended <the result>)`; a job that raised (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ends with `Error (KitArchiveIoErr e.Message)`. The handle's `cancelArchiveJob` cancels the source, which the job reads before its next file. (b) `static member onUiThread (progressed) (ended) : KitArchiveJobHost` is `posting` through Avalonia's `Dispatcher.UIThread.Post`, so a window's messages arrive on its own thread: the host the windows compose. (c) `static member immediate (progressed) (ended) : KitArchiveJobHost` runs the job on the caller's thread before it answers, with a source of its own, calling `progressed` for each file and then `ended`: the host of headless tests. (d) `static member inert : KitArchiveJobHost` runs nothing and answers a handle that does nothing: the default of scenes that run no job. (4) `KitArchiveJobState = { job : JobModel<KitArchiveFileCount>; handleOpt : KitArchiveJobHandle option }`, the one archive job a surface runs: the runner's model (`JobRunner.fs:185`) and the running job's handle. `static member idle : KitArchiveJobState` is `{ job = initModel; handleOpt = None }`; `member this.started (handle : KitArchiveJobHandle) : KitArchiveJobState` passes the job through `updateJob StartRequested` (`JobRunner.fs:233`) and holds the handle; `member this.progressed (progress : JobProgress) : KitArchiveJobState` passes it through `updateJob (ProgressReported progress)`; `member this.cancel () : unit` calls the handle's `cancelArchiveJob` while the job runs. A surface returns to `idle` when its job ends and tells the outcome in its own status, so the view binds the model's `isRunning`, `progress` and `progressText`. (5) `KitArchiveProgressIds = { bar : ConstructorUiId; text : ConstructorUiId; cancel : ConstructorUiId }` and `kitArchiveProgressView (state : KitArchiveJobState) (ids : KitArchiveProgressIds) (cancel : unit -> unit) : IView`, the one progress row of both surfaces: a `DockPanel` whose right child is a `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton` `Cancel` (`negativeBackground`, carrying `ids.cancel`, its press calling `cancel`) and whose fill is a vertical `StackPanel` of a `ProgressBar` carrying `ids.bar` (minimum 0, maximum 1, its value the progress's `fraction`, indeterminate while no progress has come) and a `TextBlock` carrying `ids.text` with `progressText`, or `Starting…` before the first file. Every id is an AutomationId. (6) The dialogs. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: the body of `KitFolderPicker.pickThen` (step 174) moves into `startPick<'Picked> (pick : Async<'Picked option>) (onPicked : 'Picked -> unit) : unit` (start `pick` with `Async.StartImmediate`, call `onPicked` with a chosen value, nothing on `None`), which `pickThen` calls, so one body starts every dialog. In `KitArchiveJob.fs`: `type KitZipPicker with static member ofWindow (owner : TopLevel) (suggested : FolderName) : KitZipPicker` (step 198): `pickZipToWrite name` is `owner.StorageProvider.SaveFilePickerAsync` titled `Send kit`, with `SuggestedFileName` the name, `DefaultExtension` `zip`, one file type `Zip archive` (`*.zip`), `ShowOverwritePrompt` true and `SuggestedStartLocation` the `suggested` folder when `TryGetFolderFromPathAsync` resolves it; `pickZipToOpen ()` is `OpenFilePickerAsync` titled `Open kit from zip`, one file, the same file type and start location. Each answers `Some (FileName path)` of the chosen file's `TryGetLocalPath ()`, and `None` on Cancel, for a file with no local path, or when the provider throws (a host without one): the IO edge in the shape of `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` (step 150) and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile` (`:3395`); it creates no folder. `member this.pickZipToWriteThen (name : FileName) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` and `member this.pickZipToOpenThen (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` are `startPick` of the two dialogs. No queue, retry or second job is added: a surface runs one archive job at a time. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs`, `module KitArchiveJobTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. `an immediate job reports each file and then its end on the caller's thread`: `immediate` over recorders, starting a job that reports 1 and 2 of 2 files and answers `Ok (KitArchiveFinished 2)`, has recorded, before `startArchiveJob` answers and on the test's thread, two progresses whose `completed` is 1 and 2 and `total` `Some 2`, then that end. `a posting job hands its cancellation to the run before its next file`: `posting` with a `post` that calls at once, over a job that reports its first file, then waits on a test-local gate and answers `KitArchiveCancelled` when its token is cancelled: once the first progress has arrived (a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep), the fact calls `cancelArchiveJob` and opens the gate, and the recorded end is `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`. `a posting run that raises ends with KitArchiveIoErr carrying its message` : a job raising `IOException "disk gone"` ends with `Error (KitArchiveIoErr _)` whose reason contains `disk gone`. `a job state runs from start through progress back to idle`: `idle` is not running and has no progress text; `started` with a recording handle is running; `progressed` of 1 of 3 files reads a progress text starting `1 / 3`; `cancel ()` calls the handle once; `idle` again is not running. `the zip pickers hand on the file the dialog answers and nothing on a cancel`: a `KitZipPicker` whose fields answer `Some` of a test-local zip at once makes `pickZipToWriteThen` and `pickZipToOpenThen` call `onPicked` once with it, and `KitZipPicker.none` never calls it.

**Acceptance.** After the job host lands, `KitArchiveJobHost` MUST run an archive job through `JobRunner.startBackground` with per-file progress and a cancel read before each file, `KitArchiveJobState` MUST follow `JobRunner.updateJob`, and `KitZipPicker.ofWindow` MUST open the save and open dialogs; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an immediate job reports each file and then its end on the caller's thread`, `a posting job hands its cancellation to the run before its next file`, `a posting run that raises ends with KitArchiveIoErr carrying its message`, `a job state runs from start through progress back to idle` and `the zip pickers hand on the file the dialog answers and nothing on a cancel`, the count rising by 5, with `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel` passing as written; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
